--- enriched_prompt (11074 chars) ---
Build a complete, premium MERN online learning platform for programming and tech courses. All courses are free. Students earn certificates by passing final exams. Admins exclusively manage all content. Check @/client/package.json and @/server/package.json for available dependencies.

---

## BACKEND — Express + Mongoose

### Models

**User**
- `name`, `email` (unique), `password` (bcrypt-hashed), `role` (`student` | `admin`)
- `avatar` (string, optional), `bio` (optional — used for instructor profiles when role is admin)
- `enrolledCourses`: [{ courseId, enrolledAt, lastAccessedAt }]
- `certificates`: [{ courseId, issuedAt, certificateId (uuid) }]

**Course**
- `title`, `slug` (unique), `description`, `thumbnail` (URL string), `category` (e.g. "Web Dev", "Python", "Data Science"), `tags` ([string])
- `instructor`: ref → User (admin)
- `status`: `draft` | `published`
- `level`: `beginner` | `intermediate` | `advanced`
- `estimatedDuration` (minutes)
- `sections`: [{ title, order, lessons: [ref → Lesson] }]
- `finalExam`: ref → Exam
- `enrolledCount` (number)
- `createdAt`, `updatedAt`

**Lesson**
- `title`, `description`, `order`
- `videoUrl` (string — YouTube embed or direct URL)
- `resources`: [{ name, url, type: `pdf`|`link`|`zip` }]
- `quiz`: { questions: [{ question, options: [string], correctIndex, explanation }] }
- `codingChallenge`: { prompt, starterCode, language, solution }
- `course`: ref → Course
- `duration` (minutes)

**Exam** (Final Exam per course)
- `course`: ref → Course
- `questions`: [{ question, options: [string], correctIndex, explanation }]
- `passingScore` (number, default 70 — percentage)
- `timeLimit` (minutes)

**ExamAttempt**
- `user`: ref → User, `course`: ref → Course, `exam`: ref → Exam
- `answers`: [{ questionIndex, selectedIndex }]
- `score` (percentage), `passed` (boolean)
- `attemptedAt`

**Progress**
- `user`: ref → User, `course`: ref → Course
- `completedLessons`: [{ lessonId, completedAt }]
- `quizResults`: [{ lessonId, score, attemptedAt }]
- `codingResults`: [{ lessonId, passed, submittedAt }]
- `overallPercent` (computed)

### Routes (prefix `/api`)

- `POST /auth/register` — register student (role defaults to `student`); hash password with bcrypt (10 rounds); sign JWT with `process.env.JWT_SECRET`
- `POST /auth/login` — verify credentials, return JWT + user object (no password)
- `GET /auth/me` — protected; return current user

- `GET /courses` — list published courses; supports `?category=&level=&search=` query params
- `GET /courses/:slug` — course detail with populated sections/lessons (no correct answers exposed)
- `POST /courses` — admin only; create course
- `PUT /courses/:id` — admin only; update course
- `DELETE /courses/:id` — admin only
- `POST /courses/:id/publish` — admin only; set status to published

- `POST /courses/:id/enroll` — authenticated student; enroll (add to user.enrolledCourses + increment enrolledCount)
- `GET /courses/:id/progress` — authenticated; return Progress doc for user+course
- `POST /courses/:id/lessons/:lessonId/complete` — mark lesson complete; recalculate overallPercent
- `POST /courses/:id/lessons/:lessonId/quiz` — submit quiz answers; store score
- `POST /courses/:id/lessons/:lessonId/challenge` — submit coding challenge result

- `POST /courses/:id/exam/attempt` — submit final exam; calculate score; if passed → auto-issue certificate (generate uuid, push to user.certificates); return { passed, score, certificate? }
- `GET /courses/:id/exam/attempts` — user's attempts for this course

- `GET /instructors` — list all admin users with public profile fields (name, bio, avatar, courses they authored)
- `GET /instructors/:id` — instructor profile + their published courses

- `GET /admin/courses` — admin; all courses (any status)
- `GET /admin/users` — admin; list all users

- `GET /users/me/dashboard` — authenticated; return enrolled courses with progress %, recent activity, certificates
- `GET /users/me/certificates/:certificateId` — certificate details for download/share

### Seed Script (`/server/src/seed.js`)
Create these users (bcrypt-hash passwords, 10 rounds):
- Admin: `admin@learnify.com` / `Admin@1234`, role: `admin`, name: "Alex Morgan", bio: "Full-stack developer and educator with 10+ years of experience."
- Student: `student@learnify.com` / `Student@1234`, role: `student`, name: "Jamie Lee"

Seed 3 published courses (with at least 2 sections each, 2–3 lessons per section, a final exam with 5 questions, passingScore 70):
1. "JavaScript Fundamentals" — beginner, category "Web Dev"
2. "Python for Data Science" — intermediate, category "Data Science"
3. "React & Modern Frontend" — intermediate, category "Web Dev"

